{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Like Mount Perazim.</b> It is the one known from the wars of David (II Samuel 5:20), which is called Baal-perazim, because suddenly the Philistines slew [them] in a wondrous deed, or like the valley [in Gibeon], which is in Gibeon:" "<b>[He will be enraged].</b> He was enraged (a hint) at the time of the standing of the sun and the moon (Joshua 10:12); so will HaShem do a strange war upon Israel such as has not been heard of like it:" "<b>His work is strange.</b> Doubled in meaning, like [the pattern of] כמשפט:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:39.331474495Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}